    "financial_health_sentiment": "Neutral",
    "valuation": "No multiples are available here to compare with peers. On price alone, the stock has given back roughly half of its spring rally, from a $64.90 weekly close in mid-June to $32.60, which removes most of the speculative premium while still sitting about twice its March level.",
    "valuation_sentiment": "Neutral",
    "growth_vs_risks": "Upside comes from a component-cycle recovery and demand from power and data-center infrastructure, which drove the spring re-rating. Risks are that the rally front-ran fundamentals, cyclical end markets (industrial, automotive) and execution on the capacity build-out. After five weeks of consolidation between $31 and $33, with the excess already unwound, the balance tips modestly toward growth.",
